Richard Russell chaired the Senate Armed Services Committee, which (jointly with Foreign Relations) held 1951 hearings investigating President Truman's firing of General Douglas MacArthur, including debates on the constitutionality of a president's authority to relieve a top military commander. This dismissal ended MacArthur's distinguished career amid the Korean War.  
