Domingo Faustino Sarmiento, an Argentine writer, described Juan Facundo Quiroga as the "Tiger of the Plains" (Tigre de los Llanos) in his 1845 book *Facundo: Civilization and Barbarism*, which contrasts civilized progress with rural barbarism.

